[\n        {\n          \"type\": \"invented_mechanic\",\n          \"quote\": \"Snatch it on the tether and there is nothing left to bring down\",\n          \"evidence\": \"[4.3] \\\"Size classes, fragile flag, compactor, crane magnet, oversized junk. All exist to serve the endgame. Every piece is one slot; the module is simply very heavy.\\\"\",\n          \"cites\": [\"4.3\"],\n          \"why\": \"The line does not just read as delicate — it states the outcome of grabbing it: the piece is gone the moment the tether takes it. No passage defines what the fragile flag does, so destruction-on-grab is a rule the writing invented. It also makes the piece unhaulable, which sits badly against the value-scales-with-mass haul the band is built on.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"contradicts_gdd\",\n          \"quote\": \"medium\",\n          \"evidence\": \"[4.3] \\\"Size classes, fragile flag, compactor, crane magnet, oversized junk. All exist to serve the endgame. Every piece is one slot; the module is simply very heavy.\\\" — the loot table nonetheless ships \\\"shattered_camera_mast 157 kg | 118,000 m (bottom third) | medium | FRAGILE\\\", and carries size classes and fragile flags on rows throughout.\",\n          \"cites\": [\"4.3\"],\n          \"why\": \"Raised once for the whole set, on this item as representative. The collision is between the document and the data file, not inside the writing: §4.3 records size classes and the fragile flag as cut from scope, and the table the game will load still carries both. The fiction stays as written where it matches the table — the flag is what the game will spawn — but the two files need reconciling.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"corrected\": {\n        \"flavour\": \"The optics head went first and the mast is holding its pieces together out of habit. Handle it gentle on the tether — and this low on the band, it is not worth much even whole.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solar_wing_spine\",\n      \"verdict\": \"pass\",\n      \"issues\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scorched_reentry_cone\",\n      \"verdict\": \"revise\",\n      \"issues\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"number_disagrees\",\n          \"quote\": \"the one most likely to come apart on the way to the deck\",\n          \"evidence\": \"The loot table carries FRAGILE as a boolean on seven rows — \\\"cracked_solar_array ... FRAGILE\\\", \\\"shattered_camera_mast ... FRAGILE\\\", \\\"torn_radiator_panel ... FRAGILE\\\", \\\"optics_bench ... FRAGILE\\\", \\\"cracked_pressure_dome ... FRAGILE\\\", \\\"telescope_mirror_segment ... FRAGILE\\\", \\\"scorched_reentry_cone ... FRAGILE\\\" — with no per-piece degree.\",\n          \"cites\": [\"4.3\"],\n          \"why\": \"The superlative claims a ranking that neither the passages nor the table contain: fragility is a flag, not a scale, and six other rows carry the same flag. The neighbouring superlative in this line — heaviest short of the module — is fine, because 1600 kg is the top row of the table and §4.3 puts the module above it.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"corrected\": {\n        \"flavour\": \"Something big came down wearing this once and it is charred through, the ablative crumbling wherever you grip. The heaviest thing you can get a tether on short of the module itself, and it comes off the top of the band already half ruined.\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":68779,"ttft_stream_ms":3239,"time_to_request_ms":322,"type":"result","duration_ms":82490,"uuid":"926b30c2-3a77-4fb6-9e41-4de99cb192e2"}
